<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm6c-taiyuan-2026-11-21 ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 6C / Unknown Payload (Taiyuan LC-9A) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
PRE-FLIGHT. LL2 id 13270554-4bdb-42ae-916f-1bb54492204f, status Go, NET 2026-11-21T03:50:00Z (Fri 20 Nov 7:50 p.m. PST), window 03:46-04:15Z, payload and orbit Unknown.
NO public LM-6C time/altitude/velocity table found. Loft: SURROGATE — the same CALT LM-3B typical GTO event table already used for lm8a-hainan and lm8a-wenchang,
  CALT &#x27;LM-3A Series Launch Vehicles User&#x27;s Manual&#x27; Issue 2011, Tables 3-5/3-6 (event time s, flight altitude km, ground range km). Family stand-in, not an LM-6C profile and not the assumed 500 km insertion.
  Cut at Stage-3 first shutdown T+615.7 s, 202.5 km, 2466.2 km. LM-6C has no third stage; the table is used only as the published-knot loft.
Source: http://www.georing.biz/usefull/LM-3A%20Series%20Launch%20Vehicles%20User&#x27;s%20Manual%20Issue%202011.pdf
Ground range IS published for that LM-3B table, so velocities are d/dt of the interpolated alt/range (rel_vel = |v| ground-relative).
One horizontal assumption: the published LM-3B ground range is laid along this mission&#x27;s constant-azimuth rhumb (LM-3B itself doglegs). Spherical rhumb, R=6371.0088 km.
Azimuth 189.52 deg is an ASSUMPTION. No hazard polygon was found for 21 Nov 03:46-04:15Z. It is the non-rotating southbound azimuth for a 500 km SSO (i=97.402 deg) from this pad: sin(az)=cos(i)/cos(lat).
  Prior LM-6C Taiyuan flights (7 May 2024 and 25 Aug 2026) were SSO. This repo&#x27;s LM-6A from the same pad point used an assumed 190 deg.
Orbit ASSUMED: 500 km circular, the published LM-6C SSO capability altitude, not this flight&#x27;s elements. The surrogate ends at the LM-3B table&#x27;s stage-3 shutdown, not at 500 km.
Pad (LL2 Launch Complex 9A): 38.858300N 111.580200E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=189.52 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-11-21T03:50:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
